airconv: hull shaders from vkd3d-shader (Wine's D3DCompile, used by games that compile HLSL at run
time) index the input control points with vOutputControlPointID directly, not with a temp register.
The relative index decoder only knew temps and crashed the converter (D3D11 and D3D12 tessellation).
Compile errors keep their message (other LLVM error types, no trailing NUL that cut the log line).

diff --git a/src/airconv/airconv_public.h b/src/airconv/airconv_public.h
index e167ae4..a1e6d95 100644
--- a/src/airconv/airconv_public.h
+++ b/src/airconv/airconv_public.h
@@ -362,6 +362,9 @@ inline std::string SM50GetErrorMessageString(sm50_error_t pError) {
   str.resize(256);
   auto size = SM50GetErrorMessage(pError, str.data(), str.size());
   str.resize(size);
+  /* neutron: some messages end in a NUL, which cut the log line (it never got its newline) */
+  if (auto nul = str.find('\0'); nul != std::string::npos)
+    str.resize(nul);
   return str;
 };
 
